# Normalize line endings so a file edited/regenerated on Linux (LF) and one
# checked out or regenerated on Windows (CRLF) never show up as "changed"
# for line-ending reasons alone. Git stores everything in the repository as
# LF; each platform's checkout can still use its native ending locally
# (governed by that machine's own core.autocrlf), but `git diff`/`git
# status` compare the normalized form, so a CRLF-vs-LF-only difference
# never appears as a real change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never text-normalize these, or line-ending conversion could
# corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.jar binary
*.class binary
